  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Laxmi vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 5 December, 2025 Author: Gurpal Singh Ahluwalia Bench: G. S. Ahluwalia Neutral Citation No. 2025:Mphc-Gwl:31754 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Gwalior Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice G. S. Ahluwalia On The 5 th Of December, 2025 Miscellaneous Second Appeal No. 8 of 2025 Laxmi Versus The State Of Madhya Pradesh And Others Appearance: Mr. Prateek Kulshrestha - Advocate for appellant. Mr. G.K.Agrawal - Govt. Advocate for respondents/Stat Judgment",
    "facts": "The facts necessary for disposal of present appeal, in short, are that on 07/07/2021 at about 3:30 p.m., the Food Safety Officer collected the samples of Namkeen which were being sold from firm Rathor Namkeen. It was found that on the back side of the house, the Namkeen is manufactured and is packed. Appellant, who was present at the time of sampling, disclosed his name as Laxmi Rathor. He also informed that the Namkeen is being manufactured for sale, and every day, 30 to 35 kg of Namkeen is NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2025:MPHC-GWL:31754 2 MSA-8-2025 manufactured by him. However, no document was produced. At the time of inspection, manufacturing of Namkeen and packing were not taking place. However, 25 packets of Ashok Namkeen Indore were found. 20 kg of besan was also found. Since the FSO had a suspicion that packing material as well as besan are of a substandard quality, therefore, sample of besan as well as packets over which Ashok Namkeen were printed were collected. In the report of Food Analyst, packets containing the print of \"AIN Namkeen Ashok Indore\" were found misbranded, whereas besan was found within norms. An information was given along with the report of Food Analyst to appellant, and he was also informed that he can prefer an appeal. However, no appeal was preferred, Laxmi vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 5 December, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/56904064/ 1 and thereafter, complaint was filed. 3. The Adjudicating Officer, after conducting an inquiry, held that appellant is guilty of misbranding the packing material, and accordingly, he was held guilty of committing offense under Section 26(2)(ii) and Section 31(2) read with Sections 52 and 58 of FSSA. NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2025:MPHC-GWL:31754 3 MSA-8-2025 5. Challenging the orders passed by the Food Safety Appellate Authority as well as the Adjudicating Officer, it is submitted by counsel for appellant that since name of his brother is also same, therefore, it appeared to the FSO that there is a misbranding, but in fact, appellant was selling Namkeen in the name of his brother. 6. Considered the submissions made by counsel for appellant. 7. Undisputedly, appellant was manufacturing Namkeen in Porsa, District Morena, whereas in the empty packets, in which Namkeen was being packed, it was mentioned as Ashok Indore Namkeen. Admittedly, neither the appellant nor his brother are based in Indore. Even if the name of brother of the appellant is Ashok, still they could not have used the word \"Indore\". They should have mentioned \"Porsa\" in place of Indore.",
    "arguments": "However, he further submitted that liberty may be granted to the FSO to take a sympathetic view by reducing the quantum of penalty.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "However, he further submitted that liberty may be granted to the FSO to take a sympathetic view by reducing the quantum of penalty.",
